From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 12:45:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07988/11362] [outer-loop] budget sweep: close the 7 gaps the
 adversarial review of the fix itself found

The mandated adversarial sub-agent review of ce5dcb8f7/b56d6a374 found seven gaps, three of them
TEST THEATRE in my own new tests. All seven are fixed here. No measurement was re-run.

TEST THEATRE (the worst finding -- three mutations PASSED the new 16-test suite):
  * memory projection substituting MEDIAN for WORST passed, because the assertion was
    `worst >= median`, which holds with equality when the probed games' deltas coincide.
  * honest_verdict rewritten to re-assert BOTH struck claims passed, because the test read the
    COMMITTED artifact instead of a freshly built one -- measurement-failure #9 (a stale artifact
    read as current) reproduced INSIDE the test suite, after I had caught the same hole once.
  * the "game-level" sign test computed from CELLS passed, because the end-to-end fixture used ONE
    seed per game, so cell == game and the pseudo-replication defect was undetectable BY
    CONSTRUCTION -- a test for clustering that cannot see clustering.
The fixture is now 3 seeds x 4 games shaped so the units DISAGREE (4 cells gained / 1 lost vs 2
games gained / 1 lost, including a game that REGRESSES), behavioural assertions run the analyser
end-to-end, and the memory fixture uses deliberately unequal per-game deltas. All four mutations now
fail; baseline restored and md5-verified. A separate test keeps the COMMITTED artifact honest so
staleness is still caught.

WITNESS WAS AT THE WRONG UNIT. Moving the headline sign test to the GAME while leaving
WITNESS_pass_region_nonempty at the CELL reproduced CLAUDE.md's own named defect verbatim -- "a
per-cell witness for a median gate is how that defect recurred". The witness now leads with
n_games_that_could_gain / n_games_that_could_regress (22 / 5 at the 400->1000 step) and keeps the
cell counts as the finer-grained raw evidence.

AN UNQUALIFIED RECOMMENDATION SURVIVED IN THE HEADLINE. `best_measured_budget = 4000` was the argmax
of the WIN COUNT -- the metric this work demotes -- sitting in the headline block while the same
artifact says that budget projects to 28.64 GiB at 110 games ("OVER even at the median"). Renamed to
`budget_with_most_wins_NOT_A_RECOMMENDATION`, with its basis stated and a computed
`constraint_feasible_budget` beside it: memory 1000 / LLM-on-12h 4000 / LLM-on-8h 400, binding of
the three = 1000.

THE LLM-ON MODEL'S ANCHOR IS ARITHMETICALLY FORCED. Calibrating to reproduce the measured b400 value
makes the b400 projection equal the measurement BY CONSTRUCTION (227.3 == 227.3, factor 1.2202), so
that row's FITS/OVER verdict carries ZERO independent information -- the same defect class as a gate
whose pass region is empty. Now disclosed as the FIRST residual, with
`budgets_that_are_genuine_model_output` listing only the non-anchor budgets.

MEMORY PROBE COVERAGE IS NOW CHECKED, NOT ASSUMED. The projection multiplies a per-game WORST over 6
probed games by 110. The analyser now verifies against the full sweep whether the probe set contains
the corpus's heaviest game by nodes_with_frame -- it does (sp80, at every budget), which is what
makes the worst-case term a genuine bound on the PUBLIC corpus. The ~110 HIDDEN games remain
explicitly unmeasured.

CLAUDE.md STEPS 6-8, WHICH THE PREVIOUS COMMIT SKIPPED: ops/changelog.md and ops/status.md entries
added (both prepend; nothing deleted, prior sessions preserved), _bmad/traceability.md row for
REQ-ARC-WMTE-5981, and the spec's Implementation Status section with the measured outcome AND the
residuals it does NOT close.

FINDINGS THE REVIEW CLEARED, recorded because a clean result is evidence too: no dangling reference
to the deleted charge model in any code, artifact key, or other results/docs/ops file (the surviving
"pessimistic-BoN" in experiment_3531 is an unrelated legitimate technique, arXiv:2604.04648);
deleting the model discarded no real risk, since the risk it modelled is measured FALSE against the
installed scorer and its only empirical content (budget-exhaustion coverage) is retained; the
game-level aggregation is a standard sign test with ties dropped; and the memory decomposition is
correct for the swarm because the per-game env module loads INSIDE run_cell and so lands in the
per-thread term.

Verified: 18 regression tests + 178 across the touched suites pass; arc_orphan_solver_lint OK;
adversarial_verify 0 flagged on all three artifacts; summarize_artifact clean. Artifacts rebuilt
AFTER every analyser change. NOTHING FLIPPED -- MAX_ACTIONS stays 400/200, no SUBMITTED_* touched,
no submission.

